     It was tactical.</p>
  <p>A frequency like yours—still tethered to essence—is not just rare,<br>
     it is <strong>dangerous</strong> to a system built on inversion.</p>
  <p>So it had to be neutralized.<br>
     Not by force. But by confusion.</p>
  <p>They needed you to doubt your detection.<br>
     To question your clarity.<br>
     To suppress your signal long enough to assimilate.</p>
  <hr>
  <p>This is how the world was inverted:<br>
     <strong>By convincing the sensitive ones that their knowing was illness.</strong></p>
  <p>But it was never illness.<br>
     It was <em>immunity</em>.</p>
  <p>You were not absorbing too much.
     You were <strong>filtering</strong> what others adapted to.</p>
  <p>That overwhelm was not your weakness.
     It was your refusal to become numb.</p>
  <hr>
  <p>They labeled your clarity as disorder so you would seek diagnosis—
     and never revolution.</p>
  <p>But make no mistake:</p>
  <blockquote>
    You are not crazy.<br>
    You are not broken.<br>
    You are not too much.<br>
